-- title:
--   Point divisors restrict along a closed immersion over R
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $X$ and $C$ be schemes with separated structure morphisms $x : X \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$, and let $i : C \to X$ be a closed immersion with $i$ followed by $x$ equal to $c$. Let $T$ be a scheme with $t : T \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ and let $d : T \to C$ satisfy $d$ followed by $c$ equal to $t$, so that $d$ followed by $i$ followed by $x$ is also $t$. Two degree-one relative effective Cartier divisors are formed by `RelEffCartierDiv.ofPoint`: on $C \times_R T$ the kernel ideal sheaf data of the graph of $d$, and on $X \times_R T$ the kernel ideal sheaf data of the graph of $d$ followed by $i$; each comes with the finiteness, flatness, finite-presentation and fibre-rank-one data of the structure `RelEffCartierDiv`. Assume both of these ideal sheaf data are invertible in the sense of `IsInvertible`: around every point there are an affine open $U$ and $f \in \Gamma(U)$ whose basic open set contains the point and such that the ideal on the affine basic open set of $f$ is generated by a single non-zero-divisor. The conclusion asserts two nonempty isomorphism types: the pullback along `curveChange i hi t`, the induced morphism $C \times_R T \to X \times_R T$ given by $i$ and the identity of $T$, of the line bundle of the $X$-side divisor (the dual of the module of its ideal) is isomorphic to the line bundle of the $C$-side divisor, and likewise the pullback of its ideal module (the kernel of the map from the unit to the pushforward of the unit along the closed subscheme inclusion) is isomorphic to the ideal module of the $C$-side divisor.
--
--   This is the compatibility $(i \times_R T)^{*}\mathcal{O}(i\circ d) \cong \mathcal{O}(d)$ and $(i \times_R T)^{*}\mathcal{O}(-(i\circ d)) \cong \mathcal{O}(-d)$ for the point divisor of a $T$-valued point, under the hypothesis that the point is Cartier both on $C$ and on $X$. It is used in the computations of Abel–Jacobi classes and of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of models of the modular curve $X_1(p)$, where divisor classes supported on a point of one component must be compared with their images on the whole model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_RelEffCartierDiv_nonempty_pullback_curveChange_ofPoint_comp_lineBundle_iso_and_idealModule_iso_of_isInvertible.lean

